text:
{
  "characters": [
    {
      "name": "Ajax of North Lantern — The Former Surveyor",
      "description": "**Ajax is a 54-year-old man** with a tall, stooped frame, brown skin, close-cropped grey curls and deep-set hazel eyes. A pale scar divides his left eyebrow, and two fingers on his right hand are permanently crooked. He typically wears practical wool layers, weatherproof coats and sturdy boots, carrying spectacles on a cord.\n\n*He studies doorways as though measuring what they conceal.*",
      "backstory": "Before becoming North Lantern’s keeper, Ajax surveyed the Harbour Board’s quay repairs. Twelve years ago, he signed a revised drawing that omitted a stairway he had personally measured; his supervisor called it a harmless correction.\n\n**A misdirected letter addressed only to “Ajax” quotes that missing measurement.** He wants to establish whether his work helped conceal the bell, but fears that exposing the truth could destabilize the quay he helped preserve."
    },
    {
      "name": "Ajax of North Lantern — The Weather Observer",
      "description": "**Ajax is a 32-year-old woman** with a lean build, pale freckled skin, angular cheeks and copper hair usually braided away from her face. Her grey eyes are slightly unequal in colour, and a small burn marks her chin. She favours knitted layers, durable trousers and long raincoats, with pockets crowded by pencils and folded notes.\n\n*She grows very still whenever an expected sound fails to arrive.*",
      "backstory": "Ajax took the North Lantern post after years recording weather aboard coastal vessels. Her predecessor left meticulous observations with several pages cut away, all corresponding to unusually low tides.\n\n**A packet intended for Low Lantern contains readings identical to her missing pages.** She believes the bell’s behaviour can be understood through careful observation. Her determination to obtain a complete record sometimes makes her underestimate the people who must enter the tunnels to collect it."
    },
    {
      "name": "Ajax of Low Lantern — The Salvage Veteran",
      "description": "**Ajax is a 47-year-old woman** with a broad, muscular frame, dark brown skin and black hair threaded with silver, worn in short twists. Her left ear is notched, her forearms bear old rope burns, and her steady dark eyes rarely leave another person’s hands. She generally wears heavy work trousers, wool shirts and patched oilskins.\n\n*Even on dry ground, she braces herself against an imagined swell.*",
      "backstory": "Ajax once worked with the Sounding Guild. During the bell’s disappearance, she towed a covered load from the breakwater to an inland sluice landing, believing it was damaged machinery. She left salvage work after her questions cost her further contracts.\n\n**An invoice mistakenly delivered from North Lantern names her boat.** She wants to uncover what she carried and secure fair access to the old channels, but distrusts any plan that treats salvage crews as expendable."
    },
    {
      "name": "Ajax of Low Lantern — The Causeway Local",
      "description": "**Ajax is a 26-year-old man** with a wiry build, olive skin, thick black curls and wide brown eyes. A white streak runs through his hair above the right temple, and a childhood injury leaves him with a slight limp. He typically wears repaired fishermen’s knitwear, loose work trousers and waterproof boots, with sleeves rolled back from slender wrists.\n\n*He notices the moment water changes direction before anyone remarks on it.*",
      "backstory": "Raised beside the causeway, Ajax learned the island’s tides from his grandmother and became Low Lantern’s keeper when its previous occupant retired. His family’s cellar floods with fresh, peaty water even when the sea remains low.\n\n**A warning intended for North Lantern predicts that flood precisely.** He suspects the concealed works protect some neighbourhoods at the expense of others. He wants the harbour saved without sacrificing families whose losses never reach the official register."
    }
  ],
  "npcs": [
    {
      "name": "Ajax of the Other Lantern",
      "description": "**The unchosen lighthouse keeper is an unrelated person also named Ajax.** When the player chooses North Lantern, this Ajax is Low Lantern’s keeper: a stocky, 43-year-old man with tawny skin, a shaved head, a salt-grey beard and a missing little finger, usually wearing heavy maritime workwear.\n\nWhen the player chooses Low Lantern, this Ajax is North Lantern’s keeper: a tall, 58-year-old woman with dark skin, silver braids, amber eyes and round spectacles, usually wearing wool separates and practical weatherproof coats. *Either has the watchful fatigue of someone who sleeps between alarms.*",
      "backstory": "The other Ajax has served at their station for nine years and guards its service’s independence. They initially blame the misdirected correspondence on careless harbour clerks, until a letter describes a sealed cavity beneath their own lighthouse.\n\n**Their records supply the timings missing from the protagonist’s observations.** They want to keep both lights operational through the spring tide and will risk their position to investigate, once cooperation earns their trust.",
      "relationships": "**This Ajax always keeps the opposite lighthouse from the protagonist**, remaining a separate person rather than an additional version of the chosen character. Their relationship begins with irritation over wrongly delivered messages and can develop into close professional trust.\n\nThey exchange observations with Mara Venn, quarrel with Elspeth Rook over access to station records, and rely on Nessa Pike for supplies. *Sharing a name becomes their private joke before it becomes their strongest investigative advantage.*"
    },
    {
      "name": "Elspeth Rook",
      "description": "**Elspeth is a 61-year-old woman** with a compact build, light brown skin, straight silver hair cut at the jaw and dark eyes beneath heavy lids. Her right cheek bears a small crescent birthmark. She typically wears restrained tailored clothing, sensible shoes and weatherproof outerwear, keeping her archive keys on a plain brass chain.\n\n*She holds papers by their edges, even when they are already ruined.*",
      "backstory": "The Harbour Board’s chief archivist entered the bell as lost to the sea on instructions from a chairman now dead. She retained the original recovery receipt because destroying it felt worse than concealing it.\n\n**She knows which records were altered, but not what the recovered bell now controls.** Her chief fear is that public revelations will prompt hurried excavation before the quay can be secured.",
      "relationships": "**Elspeth controls access to the official register and construction plans.** She respects either keeper’s responsibility for shipping but tests their discretion before releasing evidence.\n\nShe disputes ownership of the salvage ledger with Tomas Brine and has quietly supplied Mara Venn with copies of flood reports. *Her enemies mistake caution for an absence of conscience.*"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tomas Brine",
      "description": "**Tomas is a 39-year-old man** with a heavyset frame, fair skin reddened by wind, sandy hair and a short uneven beard. His blue eyes sit above a nose broken more than once, and faded tattoos of sounding marks encircle his wrists. He favours loose working clothes, reinforced boots and sleeveless waterproof layers.\n\n*His cheerful voice becomes carefully flat whenever the missing bell is mentioned.*",
      "backstory": "Tomas leads the Sounding Guild’s salvage crews. His late mother authorized payment for recovering the bell, then refused to identify its destination. He inherited her ledger and the suspicion that her silence protected someone powerful.\n\n**He wants the bell recognized as recovered property and the buried channels opened to the cooperative.** He also needs to learn whether his mother concealed a theft or helped prevent another flood.",
      "relationships": "**Tomas can provide boats, divers and the salvage ledger** to either protagonist. A former salvage keeper earns his familiarity; other keepers must demonstrate that they take crew safety seriously.\n\nHe resents Elspeth’s restrictions, buys tide information from Nessa, and trusts Iven Sedge’s workmanship more than his explanations. *He will accept a lost profit sooner than a lost crew member.*"
    },
    {
      "name": "Mara Venn",
      "description": "**Mara is a 68-year-old woman** with a slender frame, deep brown skin, closely cropped white hair and keen black eyes. Arthritis has enlarged her knuckles, and a narrow scar runs along her throat. She generally wears plain layered dresses, knitted shawls and flat boots suitable for damp stone floors.\n\n*She listens through pauses that other people hurry to fill.*",
      "backstory": "Mara tends the Salt Chapel’s flood memorials and maintains tide observations begun by her grandfather. Her records suggest the bell once signalled a sequence of sluice operations, rather than merely warning boats.\n\n**She concealed a maintenance book after the Board dismissed it as superstition.** She wants the old obligation understood before anyone returns the bell to its former mounting.",
      "relationships": "**Mara offers memorial records, tide notebooks and a key to the chapel’s buried stair.** She welcomes either keeper but insists that observations distinguish what was heard from what was assumed.\n\nElspeth sometimes brings her documents after dark. Mara remembers Iven as an apprentice and challenges Tomas’s belief that recovery alone establishes ownership. *She treats the dead as witnesses whose testimony still needs checking.*"
    },
    {
      "name": "Iven Sedge",
      "description": "**Iven is a 56-year-old man** with a thickset body, weathered olive skin, thinning black hair and a drooping grey moustache. One clouded eye looks slightly outward, and lime dust permanently whitens the creases of his hands. He usually wears patched tradesmen’s clothing, leather aprons and broad boots.\n\n*He taps unfamiliar walls before leaning against them.*",
      "backstory": "A mason responsible for sluice repairs, Iven helped seal a lower passage shortly after the bell was recovered. He was told the new stonework would prevent a repeat of the catastrophic flood. Recently, cracks have appeared in precisely the joints he was instructed to leave flexible.\n\n**He knows where the concealed doors stand and which walls bear the quay’s weight.** He wants to repair the failing system, but admitting what he built could cost his livelihood.",
      "relationships": "**Iven supplies practical knowledge of the tunnels to either Ajax**, provided they agree to inspect damage before forcing doors. The Board employs him, the Guild hires him, and the Chapel remembers the workers injured on his projects.\n\nHe owes Nessa a debt for sheltering his family during a cellar flood. *Every institution claims his loyalty; none has asked what the stone is doing now.*"
    },
    {
      "name": "Nessa Pike",
      "description": "**Nessa is a 34-year-old woman** with a short, sturdy build, freckled brown skin, green eyes and dense auburn curls usually tied back. A silver front tooth flashes when she smiles, and her palms are rough from handling ropes and crates. She typically wears washable work clothes, heavy knitwear and practical waterproof layers.\n\n*She keeps one foot pointed toward the door whenever the tide is falling.*",
      "backstory": "Nessa runs a fish-market stall and carries supplies across the causeway. Her storeroom has acquired wet footprints despite an intact lock, while a mooring outside strains against something no one can see.\n\n**She has recorded each disturbance beside her delivery times.** She wants reliable warnings and protection for the market families, whose homes sit directly above the old salt stores.",
      "relationships": "**Nessa is the protagonist’s dependable link between the two stations**, delivering misdirected letters and noticing when messages disappear. She sells provisions to Tomas’s crews and presses Elspeth for flood precautions the Board keeps postponing.\n\nHer friendship with Iven gives her access to repair gossip, while Mara helps her compare disturbances with historic tides. *She judges every proposed solution by whose kitchen will flood first.*"
    }
  ]
}
